Z||000000||Richard Parnell||04-07-2000||09:16 PM||||I know this has been asked before but I have not been able to do a search here for some months now.  I remember some one saying that you do not need a gasket for the 4 cly valve cover just a certain sealer?  Or is my partsheimers (as opposed to my allsheimers) acting up again?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-07-2000||09:52 PM||||The "Duke" engines had no gaskets from the factory. The used a permatex type of sealant. You can get a gasket for them. I would recommend a gasket. Most of the valve covers without the gasket tend to leak more often.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||04-07-2000||11:55 PM||||My 85's valve cover leaked really bad when I got it because the previous owner had over tightened it so much that the gasket broke and partially fell out. It took a while to get the cover straightened back out enough to seal. I replaced the gasket with a fel-pro one and it has not leaked any more. . . yet!||||reg||1
